<newsitem itemid="45228" id="root" date="1996-09-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: FBD half-yr pre-tax profit up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>FBD half-yr pre-tax profit up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		13.16		  vs 11.46</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.35		   vs 2.9645</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    6.92		   vs 6.12</p>
<p> Turnover		   69.05		  vs 65.77</p>
<p> Tax charge		 1.50		   vs 1.31</p>
<p> Net taxed		  5.42		   vs 4.81</p>
<p> Retained profit	  4.06		   vs 3.53</p>
<p> Record date		September 24</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 18</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 September 16</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish-based insurance and property group FBD Holdings said it had shown a capacity to grow turnover and profits in a highly competitive market.</p>
<p>&quot;Our success has been based on our commitment and ability to deliver quality services, in a cost-effective manner, to our customers. The board is confident that this progress will be maintained,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
